<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tordera (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tordera is a river of Catalonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, about 60 kilometres long, rising in the Montseny massif and reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> between Malgrat de Mar and Blanes. Its lower course marks the boundary between the comarques of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maresme">Maresme</a> and La Selva, and its valley is an important farming area. In antiquity it formed the north-eastern limit of the lands of the Iberian Laietani.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tordera-river.jpg" alt="Tordera (river)" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Josep Renalias · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Desembocadura_Tordera.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
